q q BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 169.9538 25.2 Tm (American College of Technology \(ACT\)  |  Research Synopsis  |  Page 1)Tj T* ET Q q 51.84 0 0 51.84 271.7178 748.0498 cm /Im1 Do Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 726.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13 TL/F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 153.5193 2.5 Tm (American College of Technology \(ACT\))Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 707.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13 TL/F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 166.933 2.5 Tm (Department of Computer Science)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 688.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13 TL/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 173.3248 0 Tm (RESEARCH SYNOPSIS)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 651.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 17 TL/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 6.760795 20 Tm (Adversarial Attacks and Defenses in Machine Learning-Based Financial)Tj T* 184.793 0 Td (Fraud Detection)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 632.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13 TL/F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 175.9893 2.5 Tm (Researcher: Gurmu Demuma)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 613.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13 TL/F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 213.028 2.5 Tm (October 2026)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 584.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm (Background and Rationale)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 487.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .109191 Tw 13 TL/F1 10.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 80.9 Tm (Financial fraud is a persistent cybersecurity and financial-sector problem because fraudulent transactions can)Tj T* 1.396699 Tw (cause direct financial loss, undermine customer trust, and increase operational risk. Machine learning has)Tj T* 1.651124 Tw (become an important approach for identifying suspicious transactions because models can learn patterns)Tj T* 3.164199 Tw (from large transaction datasets and support automated fraud screening. However, the security of the)Tj T* 2.915308 Tw (fraud-detection model itself is an important concern. An attacker may deliberately manipulate selected)Tj T* 2.127007 Tw (transaction attributes so that a fraudulent transaction appears legitimate to the model. Such deliberately)Tj T* 0 Tw (crafted inputs are commonly referred to as adversarial examples.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 416.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.264622 Tw 13 TL/F1 10.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 54.9 Tm (This research focuses on the security and robustness of machine learning-based financial fraud detection.)Tj T* 2.500212 Tw (Rather than considering fraud detection only as a prediction problem, the study treats the model as a)Tj T* 2.620756 Tw (cybersecurity asset that may be targeted by an adversary. The research will examine how adversarial)Tj T* .874607 Tw (manipulation can reduce the reliability of fraud detection and investigate practical defensive techniques that)Tj T* 0 Tw (can make the model more resistant to such manipulation.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 396.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm (Problem Statement)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 325.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .574633 Tw 13 TL/F1 10.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 54.9 Tm (Conventional machine learning fraud detectors are generally evaluated under normal data conditions, where)Tj T* .422673 Tw (the input is assumed to be genuine and correctly represented. In a real cybersecurity environment, however,)Tj T* 1.508759 Tw (an attacker may intentionally alter input characteristics to evade detection. A model that performs well on)Tj T* 3.770199 Tw (ordinary test data can therefore become less reliable when exposed to carefully crafted adversarial)Tj T* 0 Tw (transactions. This creates a security gap between predictive performance and operational robustness.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 254.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.136778 Tw 13 TL/F1 10.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 54.9 Tm (For a cybersecurity student, the problem is particularly relevant because it connects machine learning with)Tj T* -.026165 Tw (adversarial security, threat modeling, and defensive mechanisms. There is a need for a practical experimental)Tj T* 3.476699 Tw (study that demonstrates the vulnerability of financial fraud classifiers to adversarial manipulation and)Tj T* .53043 Tw (evaluates whether suitable defenses can improve their resilience without making the research dependent on)Tj T* 0 Tw (expensive computing resources.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 234.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.5 Tm (Research Gap and Proposed Focus)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 150.0498 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.098509 Tw 13 TL/F1 10.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 67.9 Tm (Many fraud-detection studies concentrate primarily on improving classification performance under normal)Tj T* 2.481053 Tw (conditions. Comparatively less attention is given to the security of the trained model when an attacker)Tj T* 1.603991 Tw (intentionally manipulates transaction features. This study addresses that gap by combining financial fraud)Tj T* 2.301815 Tw (detection with adversarial machine learning. The central focus is to establish a baseline fraud-detection)Tj T* 2.819245 Tw (model, expose it to realistic adversarial manipulation for tabular transaction data, and then investigate)Tj T* 0 Tw (defensive strategies designed to reduce the resulting vulnerability.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 52.8 92.04976 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.032613 Tw 13 TL/F1 10.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 41.9 Tm T* 2.861199 Tw T* .989554 Tw T* 0 Tw T* ET Q Q

